SUMMARY:LAUNCH DAY EVENT: Kathryn Stockett 'The Calamity Club'
DESCRIPTION:Kathryn Stockett\, author of The Help which became a cultural phenomenon with 15 million copies sold\, returns with The Calamity Club\, an addictive story of unbreakable women fighting to reclaim what’s theirs. \nYou will not want to miss this event at 7pm on Tuesday\, May 5\, 2026\, when the Montclair Literary Festival hosts the publication day event of The Calamity Club with Anne Burt\, author of The Dig. \n“Smart\, funny\, and driven by unforgettable characters whose opinions and actions leap off the page\, The Calamity Club is a must-read.”—Bonnie Garmus\, author of international bestseller Lessons in Chemistry. \nTickets to hear Kathryn Stockett in person start from $35 and include a signed copy of The Calamity Club. \nThe event will be held at the Unitarian Universalist Congregation at Montclair\, 67 Church St\, Montclair. Buy tickets here bit.ly/MLF-Calamity. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/launch-day-event-kathryn-stockett-the-calamity-club/
